WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.914
Training is where you choose what the model practises.

2
00:00:03.914 --> 00:00:05.893
For Ava, select navigation situations.

3
00:00:05.893 --> 00:00:11.041
For Chatbot and Device messaging, edit stories or event sequences with expected answers.

4
00:00:11.041 --> 00:00:15.000
Match the practice to the behaviour you want to explore.

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.368
In the language showcases, each line contains an input and a teaching answer.

6
00:00:21.368 --> 00:00:25.740
Use the vocabulary the model supports, and check your labels carefully.

7
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.715
The practice-edited message means Playground still uses the current weights.

8
00:00:29.715 --> 00:00:32.100
Nothing is learned until training runs.

9
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.078
Here are two device examples.

10
00:00:35.078 --> 00:00:36.856
One delivers a river update.

11
00:00:36.856 --> 00:00:41.478
The other then moves the asset to the dock without telling the hub.

12
00:00:41.478 --> 00:00:45.389
Both teaching answers are river, because that's the last delivered location.

13
00:00:45.389 --> 00:00:49.300
These labels are used for training, not supplied with Playground questions.

14
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.662
Use the training button to begin a run.

15
00:00:53.662 --> 00:00:58.009
This recording shows two real weight updates on the loaded model.

16
00:00:58.009 --> 00:01:01.565
The displayed error measures agreement with those teaching answers.

17
00:01:01.565 --> 00:01:06.308
A lower practice error is not proof of success on unfamiliar messages.

18
00:01:06.308 --> 00:01:11.050
Short pauses in this video leave time to explain the recorded result.

19
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:17.090
Ava's practice choices reset her learned weights immediately, as the message says.

20
00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:21.123
Chatbot and Device messaging add practice to their current weights.

21
00:01:21.123 --> 00:01:22.737
Each showcase saves separately.

22
00:01:22.737 --> 00:01:27.980
Read these messages before experimenting, and change one thing at a time so

23
00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.400
the outcome is easier to understand.

24
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:33.928
Choose Try this model in Playground.

25
00:01:33.928 --> 00:01:38.972
For devices, Try same messages again reuses the existing stream without adding an

26
00:01:38.972 --> 00:01:39.360
event.

27
00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.076
Here the updated model still reports river.

28
00:01:42.076 --> 00:01:45.956
That checks this case; it doesn't show a general improvement.

29
00:01:45.956 --> 00:01:51.000
Try a changed example too, and keep both successes and mistakes in view.
